// A linear value enters through a real platform boundary parameter:
// `boundary machine Main::main(handle: ImageHandle)` — the entry
// prologue's inbound argument write establishes custody, never
// inferred from zero storage. The body observes the payload then
// explicitly consumes the obligation.
use omega::language::core::drop;
public data ImageHandle [linear] { raw: addr; }
machine ImageHandle::drop(handle: &mut ImageHandle) { }
boundary trait ImageHandleRelease {
    machine release(handle: ImageHandle) reaches;
}
public data Main {}
boundary machine Main::main(handle: ImageHandle) -> i32 invokes ImageHandleRelease {
    let raw: addr = handle.raw;
    ImageHandleRelease::release(handle);
    transition raw == 0 {
        true -> zero()
        false -> present()
    }
    machine zero() -> i32 { 4 }
    machine present() -> i32 { 5 }
}
